Hi Finn,

Thank you again.

First of all, please allow me to express my apologies for asking repetitive or dull questions. I am getting my head around your explanation and have some questions. I will express them below to see if I comprehend it correctly.

In the example, the spde model predictions (which is the quantity of our interest) based on the posterior sampling are

  * INLA 23.09.09
    * Compact algorithm (Compact23)
       * Run 1: 1441.759 (1236.335, 1884.488), that is, mean (0.025quant, 0.975quant)
       * Run 2: 1444.265 (1236.825, 1883.642)
       * Run 3: 1442.572 (1235.555, 1893.085)
    * Classic algorithm (Classic23)
       * Run 1: 267.139 (180.825, 360.918)
       * Run 2: 267.773 (181.032, 362.990)
       * Run 3: 267.462 (181.479, 361.270)

 * INLA 24.02.09
   * Compact algorithm (Compact24)
       * Run 1: 1444.030 (1236.764, 1886.211)
       * Run 2: 1442.745 (1238.049, 1887.818)
       * Run 3: 1440.579 (1237.079, 1878.515)
