you can check the new version 24.04.25-1

the default behaviour is what is recommended.

use the most recent testing version. you can run with verbose=TRUE to check that
all is looking good.

Many think they are put in whatever they want and INLA will compute the correct
solution. there are cases where the posterior is so flat, like there is little
data or data with little information, that this gets very difficult. there are
nested optimizations going on, in parallel, and these cases are not that easy.

the best we are able to do, is represented in the most recent testing version.

