Hi again!

I am trying to make this model: coordinates ~ intercept + Common spatial field + scale*Specific spatial field.
Let's take the example from https://inlabru-org.github.io/inlabru/articles/2d_lgcp_multilikelihood.html#single-likelihood-version, but having common spatial field taking both "major" and "minor" nests in its likelihood, whereas the specific spatial field of minor nests would take only the minor nests.

I tried implementing with inlabru like this, and from what I understand, copy feature with fixed = F allows the scale parameter:

cmp <- ~
    common(coordinates, model = matern) +
    minor(coordinates, model = matern) +
    minor_copy(copy="minor", fixed=F) +
    Intercept(1)

lik_common <- like("cp",
  formula = coordinates ~.,
  data = gorillas$nests,
  samplers = gorillas$boundary,
  domain = list(coordinates = gorillas$mesh),
  exclude = c("minor_copy")
)
lik_minor <- like("cp",
  formula = coordinates ~.,
  data = gorillas$nests[gorillas$nests$group == "minor", ],
  samplers = gorillas$boundary,
  domain = list(coordinates = gorillas$mesh),
  exclude = c("common", "minor")
  )

fit <- bru(cmp, lik_common, lik_minor,
  options = list(
    control.inla = list(int.strategy = "eb"),
    bru_max_iter = 1
  )
)

I get the following error message: Error in fm_row_kron(M1 = M1, M2 = M2, repl = repl, n.repl = n.repl, weights = weights) :
  Size mismatch for row.kron, (n1, n2) = (1, 0)

What am I doing wrong?

Thank you and have a great day,
Edgar Lanoue

